0\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n - Common bear trigger 1 (Rates up): affects all long-duration holdings.\n   Tyler's beta of 0.809 means it falls LESS than the software complex, but\n   it will still fall. Mitigation: position cap 5%.\n - Common bear trigger 2 (Stagflation): Tyler is relatively defensive.\n - Common bear trigger 3 (AI-capex crash): Tyler is LESS exposed than\n   commercial software (government demand, not AI).\n - Tail correlation: in a 2008-style liquidity crisis, all correlated assets\n   sell off; estimated CVaR for this position: \u221245% to \u221255%\n   [Estimate \u2014 consistent with software multiple compression to 15\u201318x and\n   a modest EPS cut].\n - Contribution to portfolio tail risk: LOW given 5% weight.\n\nSECTION 8. MONITORING RULES\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nTHESIS KPIs (quarterly; breach triggers re-evaluation):\n 1. Total revenue growth \u2265 8%; recurring revenue growth \u2265 8%;\n    SaaS revenue growth \u2265 18% [Q2 2026 actual: SaaS +21.7% [Company IR]]\n 2. Non-GAAP FCF margin within guided 26\u201328% FY26 [Company guidance];\n    OWNER FCF margin \u2265 21%\n 3. GAAP operating margin \u2265 15%\n 4. Transaction revenue does NOT go negative YoY (Q2'26: +3.5%)\n 5. Buyback run-rate \u2265 $100M/quarter at prices below $425\n 6. 10Y Treasury: if > 5.2% for a month, re-run WACC scenario; if < 4.0%,\n    consider adding.\n 7. Watch: SEC filings on Kaskela investigation and ransomware lawsuit;\n    conversion of new cloud bookings to revenue.\n\nRE-EVALUATION TRIGGERS:\n - Any breach of two