ve ownership, 10% short interest, recent\n  momentum unwind, heavy SBC supply). Position size reduction: -1pp if held.\n\n================================================================================\nSECTION 6 \u2014 PORTFOLIO FIT\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTYL is a low-beta (0.809 [Aggregator \u2013 vendor]) quality compounder with\ncountercyclical revenue (government budgets are stickier than corporate IT). It\nfits a portfolio as a DEFENSIVE GROWTH sleeve, not a high-conviction growth\nholding. Its correlation to long-duration software is high (r ~0.7+ [Estimate]);\ndo NOT add it alongside other high-multiple SaaS names expecting diversification.\nIn a stagflation/recession mix (55% probability in my regime distribution),\nmission-critical government software is one of the better places to hide \u2014 but\nthe entry price destroys that protection.\n\n================================================================================\nSECTION 6.5 \u2014 KELLY SIZING\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKelly formula: f = (p \u00d7 b - q) / b, with b = (IV/Price - 1):\n- Base case: b = (324/350.73 - 1) = -0.076 \u2192 NEGATIVE edge \u2192 f = 0%.\n- Expected-value case: E[V]/Price = 331/350.73 = 0.944 \u2192 b = -0.056 \u2192 f = 0%.\n- At $295 (10% MoS): b = 0.098; p = 0.55, q = 0.45 \u2192 f = (0.55\u00d71.098 - 0.45)/\n  1.098 = (0.604 - 0.45)/1.098 = 0.140 \u2192 half-Kelly 7% \u2192 capped at 4% by macro\n  headwind and crowding \u2192 TARGET WEIGHT 4% at $295.\nLayer 5 (5%) vs Kelly (0%) gap = 5pp < 20pp \u2192 no re-analysis required, but\nconvergence at $295 is the action threshold.\n\n================================================================================\nSECTION 7 \u2014 RISKS & CATALYSTS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCATALYSTS (next 12 months):\n1. FY2026 EPS delivery vs raised guide $12.95\